v1.19 - sharing a GX with other serial drivers
  driver: candidate ports that another driver has already claimed are skipped
  instead of probed. serial-starter keeps a node under /dev/serial-starter for
  every tty it still manages, and a driver claiming a port removes it - so a
  candidate without that node is taken, not free. Probing it wrote into a
  foreign device's line; measured on a Cerbo, a heater driver sharing its port
  with Venus probe services answered 2 of 30 queries instead of 29 of 29. A
  converter that has just been plugged in is always under serial-starter, so
  nothing that should be found is lost.
  driver: the port is opened exclusively, so no other driver opens it
  underneath us while looking for its own hardware
  driver: after two polls without an answer the port is taken back from
  serial-starter once, before the restart threshold. Another driver may have
  handed it back at any time, and one call is cheaper than a service restart.

